course: dictionary
lesson: 8859
title: Shooting: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Shooting is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context. «A shooting star is not a star at all: it is a tiny grain of rock or dust.» Here the words star and rock tell you that shooting star is a special name for something in the sky.
explain: Sport gives different clues. If a sentence says «She practised shooting at the netball hoop», then shooting means throwing the ball at the hoop. The sport, the hoop and the ball are the clues. A gun would not fit there at all.
explain: A word can also be a verb, a noun or an adjective. Shooting is the -ing form of shoot, so it can describe what someone is doing right now. In «a shooting pain», it describes the pain. Ask yourself which job the word is doing in the sentence.
explain: Always check your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If «a shooting star» became «a firing star», it would not make sense, so you know the meaning is wrong.
fact: Shooting is the -ing form of shoot, so it can be a verb, a noun or an adjective.
fact: Shooting can mean firing a gun, an arrow or a similar weapon. Guns are dangerous.
fact: In sport, shooting means kicking or throwing the ball at the goal or hoop.
fact: A shooting star is a meteor: a bright streak of light in the night sky. It is not a real star.
fact: Shooting can also mean moving very fast, or recording a film or photo with a camera.
exercise: «A shooting star is not a star at all: it is a tiny grain of rock or dust.» What is a shooting star? | A real star that has fallen to Earth | *A tiny grain of rock or dust burning up in the air | A kind of football shot | A bird that flies very fast at night
exercise: Maya says, «She was shooting at the netball hoop.» What does shooting mean here? | Firing a gun | Moving very quickly past the hoop | *Throwing the ball at the hoop | Taking a photo of the hoop
exercise: If you ever find a gun, what should you do? | *Do not touch it, leave and tell an adult | Hide it in your bag | Pick it up to see how heavy it is | Fire it into the air to test it
test: Plants that are «shooting up» are doing what? | Changing colour in winter | Falling asleep | Going underground | *Growing fast
test: In the phrase «shooting a film», what does shooting mean? | *Recording it with a camera | Kicking a ball at the goal | Firing a gun at the camera | Hiding it from view
exam: Where would you most likely hear the phrase «shooting practice»? | In a library | *At a football or basketball training session | At the dentist | In a bakery
